    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d754">

                <pb facs="0838" n="726" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg726"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24172/10.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Wilson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wilson refers to the embassy’s telegram of the 21st instant, and states that
                    the governor of California has been advised of its contents. <pb facs="0839"
                        n="727" xml:id="pg727"/> Instructs him to insist that Garcia be rearrested
                    and detained for treaty period on new charge of assault with intent to commit
                    murder. Calls attention to department’s April 10, 1909,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d754-f1"/> and directs him to advise the governor of California when
                    new period of detention will expire.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
